// Unified trailing connect for list items and headings, in both their
// sugar (bracket-less) and full (bracketed) form: bare `:(args)`/
// `:{value}`/`:(){}` merges into the owner's own slots, and `:name(...)`
// attaches to the owner's own `connects` -- the same grammar a plain
// `@name` element's own groups already use.

// Sugar body: bare connect, both orders, combined in one `:`.
- content :(x: 1)
- content :{y: 2}
- content :(x: 1){y: 2}
- content :{y: 2}(x: 1)

// Sugar body: a trailing connect may start on the very next line, the
// same single-blank-line gap `skip_element_gap` grants every sigil's
// own groups. Two blank lines is too far; that shape is covered by
// `KNOWN_UNPARSEABLE`-exempt behavior elsewhere, not here, since it does
// not fail to parse -- it just stops being a connect.
- content
  :(x: 1){y: 2}

// Full-form (bracketed) list item: same bare connect support, now that
// `allow_colon_connect` is no longer disabled for the item's own groups.
- [ content ]:(x: 1)
- [ content ]:{y: 2}
- [ content ]:(x: 1){y: 2}

// Named connect on a list item, sugar and full form -- `element_list_item`
// carries `connects` now, matching a heading's own long-standing support.
- content :rule(allow:list(card))
- [ content ]:rule(allow:list(card))

// Heading sugar form gains the same named-connect support its bracketed
// form already had.
= title :rule(allow:list(card))

// Heading sugar form: bare connect, combined, matching the list-item
// sugar body above (shared implementation, `parse_sugar_body`).
= title :(x: 1){y: 2}
